<title>USA: Beard Co Q1 shr loss $0.15 vs profit $0.03.</title>
<headline>Beard Co Q1 shr loss $0.15 vs profit $0.03.</headline>
<dateline>OKLAHOMA CITY 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>THE BEARD CO</p>
<p>				 Statements of Operations</p>
<p>			(Unaudited)</p>
<p>					     For the Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							  Mar 31,   Mar 31,</p>
<p>							     1997     1996</p>
<p> Revenues					 $4,122,000 $3,146,000</p>
<p> Expenses					  4,447,000  3,854,000</p>
<p> Operating loss				  (325,000)  (708,000)</p>
<p> Other income (expense)			  (99,000)   811,000</p>
<p> Earnings (loss) before income taxes	(424,000)   103,000</p>
<p> Income taxes					     ---	 ---</p>
<p>Earnings (loss) from continuing operations</p>
<p>							(424,000)   103,000</p>
<p> Loss from discontinued real estate operations  ---   (8,000)</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss)			    (424,000)    95,000</p>
<p>Net earnings (loss) attributable to</p>
<p>  common shareholders			   (424,000)    95,000</p>
<p>Earnings (loss) per common share and common</p>
<p>  equivalent share (primary EPS):		(0.15)	0.03</p>
<p>Weighted average number of common</p>
<p>  shares outstanding			   2,799,000  2,752,000</p>
<p>SOURCE  The Beard Company</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610 NOTES: The company attributed its weaker quarterly performance to an unusual injection of pre-tax income in Q1 1996. That was attributable to the settlement of a take-or-pay contract totaling $939,000 in Q1 1996. Without the settlement, 1996 Q1 would have reflected a net loss of $836,000, or $0.30 shr.</p>
